    <!--    Nanosuit item                                                                                            -->
    <!--=============================================================================================================-->

    <string id="st_nanosuit_outfit_name">
        <text>CryNet Nanosuit 1.0</text>
    </string>

    <string id="st_nanosuit_outfit_name_s">
        <text>Nanosuit 1.0</text>
    </string>

    <string id="st_nanosuit_outfit_descr">
        <text>The Nanosuit (also known as Nano-muscle suit) is a powerful and extremely versatile set of tactical-combat armor originally designed to counter the [CLASSIFIED] threat and circumvent the technological margin between Mankind and [CLASSIFIED]. Reverse-engineered from captured [CLASSIFIED] technology, the suits' CryFibril muscle fibers can be programmed for a variety of purposes (such as hardening, muscle augmentation or camouflage), leading to drastically enhanced combat and physical performance, allowing the operator to execute superhuman feats.\n \n</text>
    </string>

    <string id="st_nanosuit_asian_outfit_name">
        <text>Korean nanosuit</text>
    </string>

    <string id="st_nanosuit_asian_outfit_name_s">
        <text>DPRK Nanosuit</text>
    </string>

    <string id="st_nanosuit_asian_outfit_descr">
        <text>The Korean Nanosuit is an advanced tactical-combat armor developed by North Korean scientists, designed to enhance the physical and combat capabilities of its operator. Utilizing proprietary nanofiber technology, the suit offers four operational modes — Armor, Strength, Speed, and Cloak — alongside robust environmental controls. It employs traditional ceramic plates to compensate for the fact that its nanofibers have difficulties contracting, a key feature required for ballistic protection. It also features cloaking capabilities, although instabilities in the system may expose the wearer due to occasional sparking. The suit features a distinctive Japanese woodland camouflage pattern. Even with its few issues, the Korean Nanosuit remains a formidable asset on the battlefield, granting its wearer superhuman abilities and increased survivability.\n \n</text>
    </string>

    <string id="st_nanosuit_2_outfit_name">
        <text>CryNet Nanosuit 2.0</text>
    </string>

    <string id="st_nanosuit_2_outfit_name_s">
        <text>Nanosuit 2.0</text>
    </string>

    <string id="st_nanosuit_2_outfit_descr">
        <text>The Nanosuit (also known as Nano-muscle suit) is a powerful and extremely versatile set of tactical-combat armor. The Nanosuit 2.0 is the second iteration of CryNet Systems' Nanosuit, replacing the older Nanosuit 1.0 four years after the latter was created.\n \n</text>
    </string>

